SUMMARY:Watercolour Fundamentals: Inspired by Botanicals: 5-Part Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Get creative during this five-week introduction to watercolour painting!\nJoin us for a five-week\, beginner-friendly introduction to botanical watercolour painting inspired by the seasonal beauty of Toronto Botanical Garden.\n \nOver five weeks\, participants will explore the foundations of watercolour\, learning essential techniques such as brush handling\, water control\, colour mixing\, layering\, and basic composition.\n \nThe course will combine technical exercises with observational painting inspired by botanical subjects and natural forms\, helping participants build confidence while developing their own creative style in a supportive and welcoming environment.\n \nTopics covered include:\n \n\n\nMaterials and watercolour fundamentals\n\n\nBrush techniques and mark-making\n\n\nColour theory and colour mixing\n\n\nLayering and glazing techniques\n\n\nBotanical studies\n\n\nNo prior experience is required.\n \nBasic materials will be available during class. Additional materials may be recommended throughout the course for participants wishing to continue practicing independently.\n \nWednesdays\, July 8 through August 5 from 6:30 to 8:30 p.m. (five sessions)\nPublic $145\, TBG Members $130 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Maria Ubeeva\nMaria Ubeeva is a Toronto-based mixed media artist with a deep passion for watercolour. Drawing inspiration from botanicals\, landscapes\, and urban scenes\, her work captures everyday beauty through expressive colour\, layered textures\, and delicate detail.\n \nWith extensive art training and years of creative practice\, Maria has exhibited her work in community art spaces across Toronto. She is also the founder of Little by Little Art\, a growing creative brand centred around prints\, cards\, and paper goods created from her original artwork.\n \nBeyond her studio practice\, Maria is a passionate educator and workshop instructor who believes creativity should feel welcoming and accessible to everyone\, regardless of experience level. Her teaching style focuses on building confidence\, encouraging observation\, and helping students develop their own artistic voice in a relaxed and supportive environment.\n \nMaria believes that painting offers a unique way to connect with nature while creating space for reflection and self-expression. Through her classes and workshops\, she hopes to foster not only artistic growth\, but also a genuine sense of community\, curiosity\, and creative joy.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/watercolour-fundamentals-inspired-by-botanicals-5-part-workshop/
